{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-26T17:19:42.879Z","author":"codex","author_source":"configured","agent_harness":"pi","agent_model":"glm-5.3:cloud","agent_model_source":"environment","agent_instance":"139192239be27480430e4428","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"glm-5.3:cloud","source":"environment"},"effort":null,"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-26T17:19:42.879Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-26T17:19:42.879Z","author":"codex","text":"Cause: pm-cli 2026.10.23 changed PmClient.get to a generic ReadPromise<GetResult, Options> signature (read-output contracts), so the recipes test hand-rolled peer-transition double (async get(id) returning Promise<GetResult>) no longer satisfied FailureFirstHost and the test build failed with TS2345 at test/recipes.test.ts(132,49).\nFix: keep the double delegating to the real SDK client but make its get wrapper a faithful generic passthrough (Options extends GetOptions & PmReadOutputOptions, forwarding id and options to reader.get); no casts, no widened double, no loosened assertions. CHANGELOG.md regenerated with the bumped pm-changelog, which now emits a Closed section for closed tracker items.\nEvidence: tsc -p tsconfig.test.json exits 0; node --test --test-concurrency=2 test/recipes.test.ts 6/6 pass; npm run release:check green locally (coverage-gate thresholds met, changelog up to date, attestation ok)."}]}],"before_hash":"207e5b746a18438522b9bf13d576b53d72aee5b39498ec6bd5d9026f883ba46a","after_hash":"92ee2cfb0e72588f256f14184f069031c1d353aa4a341ae03bc5a78794021fd4","item_hash_version":3,"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"b3abf6868332e6372929447658814eb10f71e27dd7d53aa4bef5ae5caeb108d5"}
